title: Relations with the Red General
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; red_general_timer += 4 if not staal_marcher_adopted; red_general_timer += 6 if staal_marcher_adopted; red_general_timer -= 2 if chancellor == "Staal"
view-if: (rubicon and red_general_unlock and red_general_timer <= 0 and not staal_fight) and not staal_dead
card-image: img/portraits/schleicher.jpg
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: govt_affairs
go-to: schleicher_menu if not staal_marcher_adopted; schleicher_spd_established if staal_marcher_adopted

= Relations with the Red General

[? if chancellor_party == "Marcher": While the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> remains in full control of the government for the time being, we must not get complacent. Kurt Staal certainly has more tricks up his sleeve — it is too early to ignore his ability to further influence the environment. ?][? if chancellor_party != "Marcher": While the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> remains steadfast in its commitment to a united front against the incumbent <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> government, the Greater Worker's Guild, our Free Guild, has shown some openness to an accommodation with General Kurt Staal. He has also shown interest in winning over the Free Guild through his support for public works. ?]

@schleicher_menu

- @spd_schleicher_adopted: Adopt a policy of cooperation with the Red General!
- @convince_spd_schleicher: Push the party toward a more cooperative line with Staal.
- @united_front: Reiterate our opposition against the <span style="color: #808080;">reactionaries</span>.
- @united_front_majority: Reiterate our opposition against the <span style="color: #808080;">reactionaries</span>.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@spd_schleicher_adopted
subtitle: The Free Guilds have firmly decided, but convincing the party is a whole another matter.
unavailable-subtitle: The pro-Staal factions aren't strong enough to have an impact on Greater Worker's Guild policy.
view-if: staal_marcher_support >= 10
choose-if: labor_strength + reformist_strength + social_patriot_strength >= (center_strength*1.5) + left_strength
on-arrival: staal_marcher_adopted = 1; staal_marcher_r += 1 if staal_marcher_r < 5; center_dissent += 5; left_dissent += 10; labor_strength += 10; reformist_strength += 5; staal_approval += 2
max-visits: 1

The Greater Worker's Guild leadership has now officially—although only in private—taken a stance in favor of cooperating with the "Red General." The Free Guild will attempt to leverage its influence over the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> to push our hesitant party leadership toward adopting the same position.

Gradually, a shift in opinion is becoming visible within the party. Lyle Bristol has now come out in support of making deals with the General.

@convince_spd_schleicher
subtitle: [? if chancellor == "Goodryke": It's almost impossible to argue to the party to pursue this line, at least with Goodryke as chancellor. ?][? if chancellor == "Staal": Cooperation with the General himself is not unthinkable, with his concessions made toward the Free Guilds. ?]
unavailable-subtitle: The pro-Staal factions aren't strong enough to have an impact on Greater Worker's Guild policy.
view-if: staal_marcher_support < 10
choose-if: labor_strength + reformist_strength + social_patriot_strength >= (center_strength*1.5) + left_strength
on-arrival: staal_marcher_support += 3; staal_marcher_support += 1 if wtb_adopted; staal_marcher_support -= 1 if chancellor == "Goodryke"; staal_marcher_support -= 1 if otl_heartland_coup_seen; commons_marcher -= 1; disfavored_marcher -= 1; commons_collectivist += 1; disfavored_collectivist += 1; center_dissent += 5; left_dissent += 5

Slowly but surely, the Greater Worker's Guild leadership is beginning to warm to the idea of constructive cooperation with the so-called "Red General." However, much work remains to be done—many within the Free Guild, and the overwhelming majority of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, remain firmly opposed to cooperating with the man [? if chancellor == "Goodryke": propping up the widely despised Goodryke cabinet?][? if chancellor == "Staal": who now heads a widely unpopular government?]. [? if wtb_adopted: Our adoption of the Voss Renewal Plan—and Staal’s public support for similar public works initiatives—has modestly increased the party’s willingness to consider cooperation. ?]

[? if otl_heartland_coup_seen: Furthermore, his role in the coup against our Heartland government has only deepened the animosity toward both him and the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>. ?] Rumors about our cooperation has damaged our standing among the working class.

@united_front
view-if: chancellor_party != "Marcher"
subtitle: The consensus view within the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>: we are, afer all, a democratic party.
on-arrival: staal_marcher_support -= 2 if staal_marcher_support > 0; staal_marcher_r -= 1 if staal_marcher_r > 0; staal_marcher_influence -= 1 if staal_marcher_influence > 0; commons_marcher += 2; commons_collectivist -= 1; left_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5

We continue to argue for a united opposition of the democratic parties against the unpopular [+ chancellor +] government, and win support among the people for doing so. 

@united_front_majority 
view-if: chancellor_party == "Marcher"
subtitle: Given our absolute majority in the government, we have no need of cooperating with Staal — and can instead aim to widen the united front against those who would bring the Republic down.
on-arrival: staal_marcher_support -= 2 if staal_marcher_support > 0; staal_marcher_r -= 1 if staal_marcher_r > 0; staal_marcher_influence -= 1 if staal_marcher_influence > 0; commons_marcher += 2; commons_collectivist -= 1; left_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5

We continue to decry the anti-democratic opposition as ruinous to the Republic, highlighting the role chancellor [+ chancellor +] plays in stabilizing the situation. This helps our support among the people.

@schleicher_spd_established

- @schleicher_ties: Cultivate closer ties with the Red General.
- @schleicher_distance: Distance ourselves from Staal.
- @concessions: Using our influence, demand concessions on the government.
- @easy_discard

@schleicher_ties
subtitle: More regular meetings will be held between the two groups.
on-arrival: staal_marcher_r += 1; staal_marcher_support += 1; staal_marcher_influence += 1

Regular secret meetings between the Greater Worker's Guild, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, and Staal are being held. This will aid in reducing the mutual distrust between the party and the government.

@schleicher_distance
subtitle: We will sideline his sympathizers.
on-arrival: staal_marcher_r -= 1; staal_marcher_support -= 2; staal_marcher_influence -= 1; labor_dissent += 8; reformist_dissent += 8; social_patriot_dissent += 8; center_dissent -= 5; left_dissent -= 5; knight_dissent -= 5; reformist_strength -= 4; labor_strength -= 4; social_patriot_strength -= 4

In recent months, Staal has gained significant sympathizers within the Reformist and Labor factions of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>. Sidelining them would provoke Staal’s distrust and stir dissent within their factions affected.

@concessions
view-if: chancellor == "Staal" and staal_time >= 8 and staal_marcher_concession < 2
subtitle: There's a limit to what we can demand, but we can look at our options.

[? if heartland_leader == "Staal": Bristol demands the restoration of his government in Heartland. ?]

Labor demands the restoration of their rights and welfare.

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> a cabinet reshuffle.

We may only demand one, as to not push our luck.

- @prussia
- @labor
- @cabinet_reshuffle

@prussia
title: Demand the reinstatement of our government in Heartland.
subtitle: Regain control over the Heartland police and secure participation in state government.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if staal_marcher_r < 5: We must improve our relations with Staal first. ?][? if dufour_staal_r < 5: DuFour is extremely reluctant to give back Heartland in the hands of the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span>. ?][? if not staal_post: Staal urges us to wait until the next elections. ?][? if dsu_in_gov or dsu_was_gov: Staal is firmly committed to keeping the[? if dsu_was_gov:&nbsp;former?] <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> in government. ?]
choose-if: staal_post and staal_marcher_r >= 7 and dufour_staal_r >= 5 and not dsu_in_gov and not dsu_was_gov
view-if: heartland_leader == "Staal"
on-arrival: staal_marcher_concession += 1; staal_marcher_influence += 4; staal_marcher_support += 2; staal_marcher_r -= 2; heartland_returned = 1; heartland_leader = older_heartland_leader; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 1 if pre_in_weimar_coalition_heartland; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 1 if pre_in_grand_coalition_heartland; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 1 if in_weimar_coalition_heartland and weimar_coalition_heartland < 50; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 1 if in_grand_coalition_heartland and grand_coalition_heartland < 50; pro_republic += 10; commons_marcher += 5; burgher_marcher += 5; disfavored_marcher += 3; burgher_ddp += 3; labor_dissent -= 15; reformist_dissent -= 15; reformist_strength += 15; left_dissent -= 15; heartland_police_loyalty += 0.3; banner_strength *= 1.1; banner_militancy *= 1.1; papen_strength += 1; staal_strength -= 1; dufour_staal_r -= 2; staal_approval += 1; nationalists_staal_bonus -= 2; industrialists_staal_bonus -= 1; republicans_staal_bonus += 2

Despite rejecting Bristol’s offer a few months ago, Staal has since reconsidered. With such a popular statesman on his side, his rule will gain legitimacy in the eyes of the <span style="color: #000000;">repu</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">bli</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">cans</span> and the public. Bristol, in turn, will tirelessly advocate for a pro-Staal policy within the party.

Now, with control over the democratic bulwark once again, we can reassert democratic oversight over the bureaucracy and the Heartland police force, reversing the purges enacted under Goodryke and Staal.

- @prussian_affairs
- @prussian_affairs_dvp

@labor
title: Demand more concessions for the Free Guilds, and restoration of the Commonwealth welfare system.
subtitle: Push for higher wages, the repeal of Goodryke’s decrees, and the restoration of the eight-hour workday.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if staal_marcher_r < 5: We must improve our relations with Staal first. ?][? if dufour_staal_r < 3: Staal insists DuFour would block such a decree, unwilling to undo Goodryke’s measures. ?]
choose-if: staal_marcher_r >= 5 and dufour_staal_r >= 3
view-if: not staal_labor
on-arrival: staal_marcher_concession += 1; staal_labor = 1; staal_marcher_influence += 4; staal_marcher_support += 2; staal_marcher_r -= 2; dufour_staal_r -= 1; disfavored -= 1.8; economic_growth += 0.8; inflation += 1.4; budget -= 1; commons_collectivist -= 6; disfavored_collectivist -= 6; commons_royalist -= 2; disfavored_royalist -= 2; commons_marcher += 6; disfavored_marcher += 6; commons_unionist += 2; disfavored_unionist += 2; commons_gnu += 4; disfavored_gnu += 2; commons_gnu_bonus += 4; disfavored_gnu_bonus += 2; pro_republic += 5; labor_dissent -= 40; labor_strength += 15; social_patriot_strength += 10; staal_approval += 2; industrialists_staal_bonus -= 1

The <span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span> General has lived up to his nickname: the means test for the Poorman's Pension has been abolished, and an eight-hour workday has been reinstated in select industries to "spread out" the work among more people. Funding for the Labor Ministry, gutted under Goodryke, has been restored, and welfare levels are climbing back from their absolute lows.

The downside is clear—Staal now holds significant leverage over the Free Guilds, and many workers are beginning to place their loyalty in the chancellor, rather than the party that fought to make this possible.

@cabinet_reshuffle
title: Demand a reshuffle of the cabinet.
subtitle: Staal’s cabinet remains dominated by deeply <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> holdovers from the Goodryke cabinet of barons.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if staal_marcher_r < 7: We must improve our relations with Staal first. ?][? if dufour_staal_r < 5: Staal insists DuFour would block a reorganization of the cabinet away from his <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> favorites. ?][? if not staal_post: Staal insists his government is merely a caretaker, and we must wait until after the next election. ?][? if dsu_in_gov or dsu_was_gov: Staal is firmly committed to keeping the[? if dsu_was_gov:&nbsp;former?] <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> in government. ?][? if unionist_leader == "Hughes": It’s too late now, with Hughes of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> refusing any move toward more moderate representation. ?]
choose-if: staal_post and staal_marcher_r >= 7 and unionist_in_gov and not dsu_in_gov and not dsu_was_gov and dufour_staal_r >= 5 and unionist_leader != "Hughes"
on-arrival: staal_marcher_concession += 1; staal_marcher_influence += 2; staal_marcher_support += 2; staal_marcher_r -= 2; papen_strength += 2; staal_strength -= 1; dufour_staal_r -= 3; staal_cabinet_weak = 1; disfavored -= 0.4; economic_growth += 0.2; commons_marcher += 2; disfavored_marcher += 2; commons_collectivist -= 2; disfavored_collectivist -= 2; pro_republic += 8; reformist_dissent -= 10; reformist_strength += 5; staal_approval += 1

Although many <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> figures in the cabinet have already been replaced by <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> appointees, further reform is needed to nudge Staal’s government toward a more democratic appearance.

The Finance Ministry, previously held by Sherwin Crossley, is handed over to a more neutral, non-partisan banker. The Interior Ministry and the Minister without Portfolio post are assigned to the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CPP**</span>?] moderate, Godwin Trevannon. The Agricultural Ministry is granted to Sefton Sallow, a [? if not kvp_formed and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**FCL**</span>?][? if kvp_formed: <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CPP**</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?] <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> in support of peasant homesteads.

Though these shifts may seem minor on the surface, the entry of more democratic-leaning ministers into the cabinet makes our continued support more palatable to both the party and our electorate—and subtly shifts the balance in key cabinet votes.
